{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvVX8UA7E5jfrV87z3eCZx","type":"tool_result","content":"rtl\nspec.md\ntb\n---\n# sat_adder\n\nAn 8-bit signed (two's-complement) saturating adder/subtractor. Purely combinational.\n\n## Ports\n| Port | Dir | Width | Description |\n|------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| a    | in  | 8     | Operand A, signed |\n| b    | in  | 8     | Operand B, signed |\n| sub  | in  | 1     | 0: compute `a + b`; 1: compute `a - b` |\n| y    | out | 8     | Saturated result, signed |\n| sat  | out | 1     | 1 iff the result was clamped |\n\n## Behavior\nLet `r` be the mathematically exact result (`a + b` or `a - b`, with `a` and `b` interpreted as\nsigned integers in -128..127; `r` is in -255..255).\n- If `r > 127`: `y = 8'h7F` (+127) and `sat = 1`.\n- If `r < -128`: `y = 8'h80` (-128) and `sat = 1`.\n- Otherwise: `y = r` (two's-complement) and `sat = 0`.\n\nThis must hold for every input combination, including `b = -128` with `sub = 1`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39572320-39a3-4558-8dca-8c9130aa7b90","uuid":"f9b9e04b-bdec-4cad-8dd2-59fb617a532e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:52:42.493Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"rtl\nspec.md\ntb\n---\n# sat_adder\n\nAn 8-bit signed (two's-complement) saturating adder/subtractor. Purely combinational.\n\n## Ports\n| Port | Dir | Width | Description |\n|------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| a    | in  | 8     | Operand A, signed |\n| b    | in  | 8     | Operand B, signed |\n| sub  | in  | 1     | 0: compute `a + b`; 1: compute `a - b` |\n| y    | out | 8     | Saturated result, signed |\n| sat  | out | 1     | 1 iff the result was clamped |\n\n## Behavior\nLet `r` be the mathematically exact result (`a + b` or `a - b`, with `a` and `b` interpreted as\nsigned integers in -128..127; `r` is in -255..255).\n- If `r > 127`: `y = 8'h7F` (+127) and `sat = 1`.\n- If `r < -128`: `y = 8'h80` (-128) and `sat = 1`.\n- Otherwise: `y = r` (two's-complement) and `sat = 0`.\n\nThis must hold for every input combination, including `b = -128` with `sub = 1`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
